// VS Code: install the "httpYac" extension (anweber.vscode-httpyac), not the
// more popular "REST Client" - REST Client doesn't read http-client.env.json
// (it wants env vars in .vscode/settings.json instead), httpYac does.
// Pick an environment via the status bar / "httpYac: Select Environment".
// Secrets (wifiSsid/wifiPassword) live in the gitignored
// http-client.private.env.json, auto-merged over http-client.env.json - copy
// http-client.private.env.json.example to http-client.private.env.json and
// fill in real values.

// simulated-device-123 = HomelabBrain.DeviceSimulator's fixed id - answers these for real when
// AppHost is running (default IncludeDeviceSimulator=true). Swap for a real device's
// chip-id to talk to actual hardware instead.
@deviceId = simulated-device-123

### Liveness

GET {{HostAddress}}/healthz

### Readiness

GET {{HostAddress}}/readyz

### OpenAPI contract (Development only)

GET {{HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json

### Get device config

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/devices/{{deviceId}}/config

### Set WiFi credentials (device reboots on success)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/devices/{{deviceId}}/config/wifi
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ssid": "{{wifiSsid}}",
  "password": "{{wifiPassword}}"
}

### Set MQTT broker (device reboots on success)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/devices/{{deviceId}}/config/broker
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "host": "10.0.129.7",
  "port": 1883
}

### Set plant id (applied live, no reboot)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/devices/{{deviceId}}/config/plant-id
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plantId": "basil-1"
}
